From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dwc3-exynos: defer glue probe until DWC3 core is ready

of_platform_populate() registers the DWC3 child before its driver has
necessarily finished probing. If platform_get_drvdata() returns NULL, the
glue probe jumps to populate_err with ret still zero, reports success and
never retries. dwc3_exynos_otg_init() then never runs, leaving ConfigFS
gadgets bound but the UDC permanently "not attached"; the shutdown path
also dereferences the missing OTG state.

Return -EPROBE_DEFER for this case so the glue probe retries after the
DWC3 core driver is ready.
---
diff --git a/soc/gs/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-exynos.c b/soc/gs/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-exynos.c
index 3f96b06..b1a4f62 100644
--- a/soc/gs/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-exynos.c
+++ b/soc/gs/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-exynos.c
@@ -1299,7 +1299,9 @@ static int dwc3_exynos_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	dwc3_pdev = of_find_device_by_node(dwc3_np);
 	exynos->dwc = platform_get_drvdata(dwc3_pdev);
-	if (exynos->dwc == NULL)
+	if (exynos->dwc == NULL) {
+		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		goto populate_err;
+	}
 
 	/* dwc3 core configurations */
 	pm_runtime_allow(exynos->dwc->dev);
-- 
2.48.1
